    ['id' => 'people', 'title' => 'People register and the employee card', 'body' => [
      'People (HR › HR settings › People): every Golden A/S employee, with or without a portal account. The filter row above the list searches by Latin or Greek name, employee code, e-mail or job title and filters by discipline, employed / left / everyone, technical or not, employment kind, country, contract type, with or without account; the counter shows matches / total. ➕ Account next to a person without an account opens the account form pre-filled from the card and links the two on save. 📜 opens the full leave history of the person; 🪪 opens the card.',
      'The employee card is one record per person that stays for life. Tabs: 🪪 Data — identity, department, job title, contract, hiring date, prior service, marital status, working days, children (number and birth years — they drive maternity / paternity and the child allowance), jurisdiction (GR / IT rule set), employment kind (employee / contractor), and Personal data (HR only: personal e-mail, phones, home address, date of birth, AMKA, ΑΦΜ, ΔΟΥ, ID, passport, IBAN, bank, emergency contact, father\'s / mother\'s / spouse name, nationality, birth place, blood group, education, grade, transport, work phone and extension, postcode / city / country, gross salary, ΟΑΕΔ benefit, payroll code). 📑 Employment periods — Hiring, Contract change, Termination, Re-hiring events with documents; the off-boarding checklist appears under a termination. ✅ HR requests — the requests of this person, with approve / reject in place. 💬 Messages with HR — the private thread. 📎 Documents — everything filed on the card (contracts, certificates, training certificates, evaluations). 🗓 Entitlements — the balance engine per year and type, with lock / unlock and the carry-over. 🏷 Leave types — types switched off for this person. 🎓 Training — the training record and certificates. 📈 Evaluations — the annual evaluations and the evolution chart. 🕘 Changes — the audit trail (who changed what, when; secrets masked).',
      'Service: the portal computes the service at Golden A/S from the employment periods, adds the prior service at other employers (years + months on the card) and shows the total; the leave engine uses the total for the seniority steps. Keep the prior service as the accountant\'s register states it.',
      ['ul' => ['Documents: PDF, images, Word, 15 MB each, stored outside the web root; only HR / administrators and the person himself can open them. Kinds: contract, hiring form, termination notice, ΕΡΓΑΝΗ form, identity / permit, certificate, training, evaluation, other.', 'Deleting: the last employment event can be deleted while it has no documents; a card is never deleted — mark the person as left.', 'Portal account and card: one account ↔ one card. The approver of the person is the personal manager of the account, else the manager of the discipline (Settings › Portal accounts / Disciplines); the department head is the fallback for people without an account.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'imports', 'title' => 'Imports — register, personal data, prior service, balances, past leave', 'body' => [
      'Departments are the portal disciplines (Settings › Disciplines, administrators) — one list for accounts, Planning and HR; if an import ever produced a duplicate, an administrator merges it there (Merge into…), nothing is lost. The import matches department names loosely and creates a new discipline only when you tick "create unknown departments" on the preview. The pre-filled template (People › Excel template) exports every field of every card exactly as stored — the personal / payroll columns only when you are signed in as HR or Owner (a plain administrator gets the 22 general columns). The import preview warns when a file carries personal columns the signed-in account cannot write. All imports are on HR › HR settings › People / Import and take Excel files with a header row; the portal shows a preview and applies only when you confirm. Existing people are recognised by Greek name, Latin name or e-mail and updated; empty cells never erase data; unknown departments are created and flagged.',
      ['ol' => ['People register (Import people from Excel): download the template first — it is pre-filled with the current people and carries every card column, personal and payroll data included (father\'s / mother\'s / spouse name, nationality, passport, blood group, education, grade, transport, phones, address, AMKA, ΑΦΜ, ΔΟΥ, ID, IBAN, bank, gross salary, ΟΑΕΔ benefit, payroll code). An invalid value (a 10-digit AMKA, a wrong IBAN check digit) is skipped with a warning and the rest of the row is saved. The Latin name must be exactly the name on the card, otherwise a second card is created — fix the spelling in the sheet before applying.', 'Prior service: the same import; columns Prior service (years) and (months) as the accountant\'s register states them.', 'Balances (Import balances): the accountant\'s balances per person and type for a year, with "Balances as of <date>" — the cut-over date. From that date the engine counts only the records after it; everything before is in the imported opening balance, so nothing is counted twice. Use it once at go-live and whenever you re-align with the accountant.', 'Past leave records (Import leave records): Email / names, Type code, From, To, Days, Hours, Status, Reason — for history; rows already in the portal are skipped. Records before the cut-over date are "history only" and do not touch the balance.', 'Staff list of the planning board (Import Excel matrix on Planning): absences per day for a month — used by the PMs; not an HR import.']],
      'Watch for: a negative available balance after an import almost always means the opening balance already contained days that are also present as 2026 records — set the cut-over date to the date of the accountant\'s balance and re-import.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'types_rules', 'title' => 'Leave types, rules and the balance engine', 'body' => [
      'Leave types (HR settings › Types): code, name in five languages, kind on the board, counts against the entitlement, reason required, unit (days or hours), HR only (no manager stage — sick, parental, strike, paternity …), document required, paid, consumes annual leave (hour types: 8 hours = 1 day), maximum per year (statutory caps: PAT 14, MAR 5, CAR 5, FMJ 2, SCH 32 h …), once per birth (maternity / paternity), transferable or not. Built-in types are renamed only; delete only unused ones. A type can be switched off for one person on the card › Leave types.',
      'Rules (HR settings › Leave rules, validated with the accountant): annual leave is computed automatically — in the calendar year of hiring the full-year days pro rata to the days worked; 21 days in the second calendar year, 22 from the third; 25 after 10 years at Golden A/S or 12 years of total service; 26 after 25 years; 5-day and 6-day week variants; the Italian rule set for the branch; contractors have no statutory allowance. The card › Entitlements shows per type the statutory basis, the computed days, the mode (🔒 automatic / 🔓 fixed by HR), taken, pending and available. Unlock to type a different figure; lock to return to the engine. Carry-over: the unused days of the previous year are carried according to the rule (transferable types only) — the Entitlements tab has the carry / transfer action per person.',
      'Maternity / paternity: once per birth; the children\'s birth years on the card tell the engine which birth a request belongs to; days already taken at another employer for the same birth are deducted ("taken elsewhere" on the request). Other types are not transferable between employers.',
      ['ul' => ['Early leaves / late arrivals (EARLY) and any other hour type marked "consumes annual leave" are a company permission, not a statutory leave (Greek law grants annual leave in working days only): the hours accumulate and only each completed 8 hours takes one day of annual leave — the remainder is shown under the annual balance on My leave ("4 h accumulated · 4 h to the next day") and waits for the next hours; at year end decide with the accountant whether a remainder is waived or charged. Write the rule in the work regulation.', 'Days are always working days: weekends and the public holidays of the person\'s work calendar are never charged (Settings › Work calendars; a year nobody generated falls back to the country\'s public holidays, Orthodox Easter included).', 'Hour types (EARLY, SCH …) accumulate in hours; every 8 hours consume one day of annual leave where the type says so.', 'Balances per person and year are visible to the person on My leave and to the managers for their people.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'requests', 'title' => 'Requests and approvals', 'body' => [
      'The employee requests leave on My leave (type, dates or hours, reason, document when the type requires it); the manager approves or rejects (HR-only types skip this stage); HR approves or rejects; on approval the portal writes the days to the Planning board (one entry per working day with the type and reason) and the balance moves from pending to taken. Each step notifies the next person and the employee. HR can also enter a request on behalf of an employee (HR requests › New request for …) — for sick leave with the certificate, for leave agreed verbally — and can cancel or correct a record from the card › HR requests.',
      ['ol' => ['HR requests page: the queue shows the requests at your stage first (pending HR), then the manager stage, with the balance of the person next to each request; filter by year and status; per-person history from 📜.', 'Decide with a note — the note goes to the employee. A rejection returns the days to the balance; a cancellation by the employee is possible while the request is pending.', 'Documents attached (medical certificates …) are visible to the employee, the approver and HR only.', 'The same page carries the Training applications queue and the Evaluations of my people (for managers — HR sees everyone).']],
      ['fig' => 'flow-timesheet.svg', 'cap' => 'The approval ladder — requested by the employee, manager, HR, then the board'],
      'Managers may also take the manager-stage decision from the Golden PM app on their phone, after entering their authenticator code; the portal records it as a normal decision with the suffix "(mobile app)" and notifies HR as usual. The HR stage, decisions on behalf of an absent manager and HR-only types are decided in the portal only.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'leaves', 'title' => 'Leaves page — who is away, leave periods, company closures', 'body' => [
      'HR › Leaves: who is away over any period (up to three months) for the whole company or one discipline — a day matrix with the leave-type code per person and day (gold = pending), totals per type and person-days; the previous / next month buttons move the window; the assistant box answers questions about the matrix.',
      'Leave periods / groups: HR creates a period (name, type, dates, target: whole company / disciplines / people, maximum people, note, status). Open periods appear on My leave of the people targeted; they join with their own dates inside the period; the manager approves; the request is then approved automatically and lands on the board. Assign to all creates an approved record for everybody targeted at once (people with an overlapping request are skipped and listed); Undo removes what Assign to all created (never what people joined themselves); 🔄 Recount days recomputes the days of an applied period without weekends and holidays and rewrites the board.',
      'Company closure: tick "Company closure" on a period for leave the company imposes (Christmas week, August). Staff see it as 🔒 Mandatory on My leave with "assigned by HR" and cannot join or opt out; you assign it with Assign to all. The days are charged to the annual leave as working days only.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'training', 'title' => 'Training and certificates', 'body' => [
      'HR › Training: publish a training — kind introductory (new hires), internal (given by Golden A/S) or external (provider, trainer, location) — with dates, hours, places, apply-by date, cost, whether a certificate is issued, who is invited (whole company, disciplines or chosen people) and the programme. Saving an open training notifies the people invited; they apply from My leave › Training opportunities; applications reach you and the person\'s manager (HR requests › Training applications) — approve or reject, the employee is notified. You can also add people directly (approved).',
      ['ol' => ['After the training: open it, set each participant to attended / absent, type the result (Pass · 85 %), and for trainings with a certificate the number, issue date, valid-until date and upload the scanned copy — it is filed on the card › Documents as kind "training".', 'Certificates expiring within 90 days show on the HR dashboard and on the Training page: plan the refresher training before they expire.', 'The employee card › 🎓 Training shows the record with the participation summary (trainings attended, hours, certificates, evaluations); the employee sees the same on My leave › My trainings.', 'Close the training (status Completed) when everything is recorded; Cancelled keeps the record but hides it from the opportunities.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'evaluations', 'title' => 'Annual evaluations', 'body' => [
      'One evaluation per employee and year, written by HR (card › 📈 Evaluations) or by the manager (HR requests › Evaluations of my people › the person): eight criteria scored 1–5 — quality of work, productivity, technical skills, teamwork, initiative, reliability, safety & procedures, communication — the overall score is the average; strengths, areas to improve, goals for next year, training needs, comments. Draft is visible to HR and the manager only. Final notifies the employee, who reads it on My leave › My evaluations, may add a comment and acknowledges it (status Acknowledged, logged in the card changes). Once final only HR can change it.',
      'Two criteria are computed by the portal and included in the overall score: Training participation (trainings attended and hours in the year, ranked among active colleagues — top 20 % = 5, next 20 % = 4, next 30 % = 3, rest = 2, none = 1) and Attendance & consistency (starts at 5; −1 per 16 h of early leaves / late arrivals, −1 per 3 days of unplanned absence — unpaid or other absence; sick leave is shown but not penalised —, −1 per 3 leave requests asked less than 2 days ahead). The form shows them read-only with the figures behind them, and the targets of the year with their achievement. Every employee sees the same rules and his computed scores so far on My leave › How we evaluate you.',
      'The Evolution chart on the tab shows the overall score per year with the participation line (trainings attended, hours, certificates) — use it in the yearly review meeting and to feed the training programme (the training-needs text of every final evaluation is your list for next year).',
      ['ul' => ['Recommended calendar: managers write drafts in November, HR reviews in December, finals and employee acknowledgements by 31 January.', 'Keep the scoring scale consistent across managers: 3 = meets expectations; reserve 5 for outstanding, documented cases.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'targets', 'title' => 'Targets for departments and individuals', 'body' => [
      'HR › Targets: the targets of the year for the company, each department and each person — title, how it is measured, the target value and unit, due date, weight 1–5 (importance in the evaluation), progress % and status (open, on track, at risk, achieved, missed, cancelled), description and closing remarks. You manage all of them; a manager manages those of his disciplines and his people. Creating a target notifies the people concerned; everybody sees the targets that concern him on My leave › My targets and updates the progress of his own — achieved / missed are set by the manager or by you at year end. Every update is logged (History under the target). The evaluation panel of a person sums his targets (achieved, average progress).',
      'Assistant: ✨ Propose on the Targets page drafts 4–6 SMART targets for a department or a person from the facts in the portal — people and roles, last year\'s targets and results, trainings, computed scores, the last evaluation — plus your brief; Add each with one click or Edit it first. On the evaluation panel ✨ Draft the evaluation proposes scores and texts from the year\'s facts for you to review; Ask answers questions about the person\'s year. Both need the pages Evaluations and Targets enabled under Settings › Assistant › Pages; personal and payroll data are never sent.',
      ['ol' => ['January: set the company targets (HR / management) and ask every manager to enter the department and individual targets of his people by end of January — SMART: measurable, with a due date.', 'Quarterly: filter the year, sort out the at-risk ones, remind the managers to update the progress.', 'November: close the targets (achieved / missed with the closing remark) before the evaluations are written.', 'The "How we evaluate you" note at the bottom of the page is what every employee reads on My leave — write there what the company expects this year, how the prize and the ranking work.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'assistant', 'title' => 'HR Assistant — guided flows approved by HR (R67-001)', 'body' => [
      'HR › HR Assistant is a guided, step-by-step way to collect data without e-mails and Excel sheets: the person fills the flow, the portal validates every value at entry, and nothing reaches the employee card before HR approves. The first flow is "My card": every employee with a card linked to his account completes or corrects his own personal data. The hiring, leaving and dismissal flows follow on the same engine (R67-002 / R67-003).',
      ['ul' => [
        'What the employee can propose: names, date and place of birth, nationality, gender, marital status, children; personal e-mail, phones, address, emergency contact; AMKA, ΑΦΜ and tax office, ID / passport, IBAN and bank, blood group; education, transport, work phone. What stays with HR only: gross salary, payroll code, ΟΑΕΔ benefit, grade, hiring date, prior service, contract, department.',
        'Validation at entry: AMKA 11 digits whose first six are the date of birth, ΑΦΜ with its check digit, IBAN check digits, plausible dates, children\'s years as four-digit years. A wrong value cannot be submitted.',
        'Assistant: on each step the employee can write his details in his own words or photograph his ID card / passport; the assistant proposes values for that step only, the employee presses Use per value, and the photo is not stored (the scan goes to the Documents step). The page "HR Assistant" must be enabled in Settings › Assistant › Pages for the staff who should have it.',
        'Security: the identification numbers of an open flow are stored encrypted (libsodium, key derived from the instance and a random salt in cp_settings) and decrypted for the owner and HR only; the identification step and the submission ask for the authenticator code when the account has 2FA; the GDPR notice (controller, purpose, legal basis, recipients, retention, rights) is accepted on the first step and the acceptance is logged with time and address.',
        'To review: HR › HR Assistant lists the submitted flows (badge on the menu, list on the HR dashboard). Open one: every proposed value is shown next to the card value with its source (employee / assistant / document). Per field: ✔ approve or ✖ reject with a note. For the flow: "Approve & apply" writes every field not rejected to the card through the normal card save (the change log on the card shows "HR Assistant HRA-…"), files the documents under the card\'s Documents tab and notifies the employee; "Return for corrections" sends it back as a draft with your note; "Reject" closes it.',
        'Housekeeping: a draft idle for 7 days and a submission waiting for 3 days are reminded once a day; the staged values and files of applied, rejected or withdrawn flows are deleted 90 days after the decision — the flow row and its log stay.',
        'Flow templates (HR › HR Assistant › Flow templates): steps, fields per step, required fields, documents per step and approvers per flow kind and per branch (* or GR / GIT), as JSON. Only the fixed catalogue of employee fields is accepted; the built-in default is used when no active template exists.',
      ]],
      ['tip' => 'Ask the staff to complete their cards before the payroll import: HR › People shows who has no personal data, and every employee sees the completeness of his card on My leave with the button to start.'],
